<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Karen</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Karen-Pahlav, Karenids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Karen was one of the seven great noble families of Parthian and Sasanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, with lands centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahavand">Nahavand</a> in Media. Its members served as generals and ministers, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukhra">Sukhra</a>, the power behind the throne in the 480s. After the Arab conquest a branch, the Qarinvandids, ruled the mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabaristan">Tabaristan</a> until the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazyar">Mazyar</a> in 839.</p></div>
